    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily into volume and situational speed advantages, with **James Wood** (76.28) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) standing as our premier plays. **James Wood** capitalizes on an ideal setup against Chandler, combining a high xwOBA (0.420) with a slow opposing pitcher who incentivizes his high-upside speed profile. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive 14% boost due to a dynamic platoon advantage against Mahle and a favorable spot in the two-hole. **Brice Turang** (75.06) rounds out our elite tier, as his leadoff status and the matchup against Rodriguez provide the highest floor for stealing bags, our scarcest category.\n\nStrategic adjustments for today prioritized platoon and park factors over raw historical pedigree. We are leveraging the hitter-friendly environment for **Kyle Karros** (56.82) despite a neutral platoon, as the 14% park boost pushes his efficiency into startable territory. Conversely, the toughest bench decision was **Travis Bazzana** (50.71), who narrowly missed the cut. While his lead-off spot provided intrigue, the negative platoon impact of facing a left-handed starter in Murphy significantly depressed his output compared to the high-efficiency ceiling of our primary utility play, **Isaac Paredes** (62.70). **Austin Riley** (48.31) also remains sidelined, as his low-order placement and poor SP skill matchup against the formidable McLean make him a risk we aren't willing to take with our remaining game caps.\n\nRisks for the slate are relatively contained, though users should monitor the wind for **Alex Freeland** (56.60), as his score relies partially on favorable gusts to boost his utility. **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll** are locked into solid starts, though **Corbin Carroll** carries slight downward risk due to the presence of an elite hold-pitcher, potentially capping his stolen base attempts against Sproat. We are tracking the full roster carefully, specifically ensuring that **Jose Caballero**, **Trevor Story**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte** remain prepared for pinch-hit or defensive replacement duties should weather or late lineup shifts necessitate an emergency pivot.",
